<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Luis Vernet</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1791">1791</a>–<a href="/years/1871">1871</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Louis Vernet</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Luis Vernet was a merchant born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamburg">Hamburg</a> who settled in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenos-aires">Buenos Aires</a> and in 1828 founded a settlement at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/port-louis">Port Louis</a> on East Falkland. In 1829 the United Provinces of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-de-la-plata">Río de la Plata</a> appointed him political and military commander of the islands. His seizure of American sealing ships in 1831 provoked a raid by the USS Lexington, and the British reasserted control of the islands in 1833.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/luis-vernet.jpg" alt="Luis Vernet" width="302" height="392" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tochter von Luis Vernet · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vernet_Luis_Portrait.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
